# L §5.16 (round 12): a random fact's "rows and rules give samples of one type, quantities of unit U or keys of one
# index (each a discrete over it); a mix is refused (LOAD-UNIT)". g's rows are discrete over ks in 2026 and over js in
# 2027. (Was REFCORE-UNSPECIFIED §5.16, writer 5's T-73.)
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-10-18
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
index ks = [ka, kb]
index js = [ja, jb]
input w[k in ks]: num
input u[j in js]: num
input g: dist

version v1
  cite s
  governs 2026
  known 2026-01-01
  w[ka] = 1
  w[kb] = 1
  u[ja] = 1
  u[jb] = 1
  g = discrete(w[k] for k in ks)

version v2
  cite s
  governs 2027
  known 2026-01-01
  g = discrete(u[j] for j in js)

ask q: share(g == ka) law 2026-06-30 paths 10 seed 1
=== expect
refused: LOAD-UNIT random fact g mixes sample types: discrete over js, ks ...
